   "text_reread": "\"Its page of race bibliography will be especially helpful to students and study club workers.\"\nPAULINE SMITH,\nDetroit, Mich.\n\n\"THE CRISIS fills a long-felt want. It should be indispensable to every patriotic American.\"\nR. C. EDMONDSON,\nWashington, D. C.\n\n\"I have just read the last issue of THE CRISIS. I find it valuable for the series of facts that it presents in succinct form. I have read it with deep interest and consider it of distinct value.\"\nWILBUR P. THIRKIELD,\nPresident Howard University,\nWashington, D. C.\n\n\"I like THE CRISIS. This first number is good in itself, and is full of great promise.\"\nCHARLES T. THWING,\nPresident Western Reserve University,\nAdelbert College,\nCleveland, Ohio.\n\n\"It makes a dignified, informing and convincing argument against color prejudice.\"\nSAMUEL A. PEASE,\nAttorney, Brooklyn.\n\n\"I feel that it supplies a long-felt necessity. I am trying to induce all lovers of fair play for the human race to subscribe to it.\"\nT. M. DENT,\nDept. Commerce and Labor.",
