   "text": "\"I am much impressed with the appearance of your new monthly magazine.\"\nL. J. JOHNSON,\nHarvard University,\nCambridge, Mass.\n\n\"The paper is excellent and I hope I may be instrumental in securing other subscribers.\"\nBERTHA JOHNSTON,\nBrooklyn, N. Y.\n\n\"It is a splendid effort, courageous in its utterances and manly in its defense of the man of color.\"\nGEO. E. WIBECAN, JR.\nBrooklyn, N. Y.\n\n\"I read the first number of your magazine, THE CRISIS, with care and much appreciation yesterday.\"\nW. H. SHORT,\nExecutive Secretary,\nThe Peace Society of the City of New York.\n\n\"I have read every word of the first number of THE CRISIS with a relish equal to the zeal of the production.\"\nJ. WILBUR NORRIS,\nSioux City, Ia.\n\n\"I have looked over the matter arranged for THE CRISIS and it all seems to me to be excellent. I cannot suggest any change. I shall be glad to contribute to the magazine.\"\nCHARLES EDWARD RUSSELL,\nNew York.",
